<!--
    Region-based (Phoenix/SAILR) structurer - loop-successor REFINEMENT
    infrastructure (option `regionlooprefine`, default OFF).  Sits on top of
    `regionstructure` (DIV-12 default-on): the read side of angr
    `RegionIdentifier._refine_loop_successors_to_guarded_successors` /
    `_ensure_jump_at_loop_exit_ends` (the `force_loop_single_exit` path).

    What this proves end to end:

      * `KunaRegionIdentifier::cyclic_loops()` projects each identified cyclic
        region onto basic-block start addresses (head / refined loop body / exit
        frontier) and hands it to the S8 structurer.
      * For a MULTI-EXIT loop the base cyclic schemas (`try_fold_loop`) decline,
        `region_structurer::refine_loop_edges` fires (it virtualizes the loop's
        SECONDARY exits to gotos so the body collapses to a single-exit shape) -
        confirmed live via `KUNA_RS_DEBUG=1` (`[rs] RI loop head=...` +
        `[rs]   refined loop head#N`).

    `mexit` is a multi-exit loop (a `for` with an early `return -1` AND a
    `break`/`return s`), x86-64 GCC -O1, the `.text` bytes of a `-c` object
    loaded at 0x401000.  Source:

        int mexit(int n, int *a) {
            int i, s = 0;
            for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if (a[i] < 0) return -1;   // early-return exit (secondary)
                if (a[i] == 7) break;      // break exit (secondary)
                s += a[i];
            }
            return s;
        }

    PARITY PROOF (the honest infrastructure-increment result): the refinement is a
    strict SUPERSET of the base structurer - a loop the base schemas already fold is
    untouched, and a multi-exit loop the base schemas decline still falls back to
    `CollapseStructure` for the FINAL collapse when the acyclic convergence is
    incomplete (the structurer reports `ok=false`, so the upstream Ghidra path emits
    the C).  The net effect on emitted C is therefore ZERO: pass 1
    (`regionlooprefine off`) and pass 2 (`regionlooprefine on`) emit byte-identical
    C - the same clean `do { ... } while (...)` with the two early returns inside and
    ZERO gotos.  Turning the opt-in ON exercises the new RI-projection +
    `refine_loop_edges` machinery (it FIRES on this multi-exit loop) without changing
    output, which is exactly the parity invariant this increment lands: the
    refinement infrastructure is wired in and active, byte-safe by construction.

    The remaining work to convert "refinement fires" into an actual goto REDUCTION
    (so refined loops fold to a structured root instead of falling back) is the
    acyclic-schema completion + continuation hoisting documented as the next
    increment in docs/region-structurer-roadmap.md (Inc 6).

    Asserted invariants below hold across BOTH passes (counts are 2x the per-pass
    count): the do-while body, the two early returns, the loop-exit condition, and
    ZERO gotos - identical with the refinement off and on.
-->
